<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lex Flavia Malacitana</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 81–84</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Lex Flavia Malacitana is the municipal charter of Malaca (Málaga) in the Roman province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispania">Hispania</a> Baetica, issued under the emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/domitian">Domitian</a> around 81–84 CE. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bronze">Bronze</a> tablets bearing it and the charter of nearby Salpensa were found near Málaga in 1851. Its rules on elections and magistrates are a major source for Roman town government in the provinces.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lex-flavia-malacitana.jpg" alt="Lex Flavia Malacitana" width="320" height="221" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Stgoetz · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lex_malacitana_ch_56.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
